{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527673-have-you-ever-managed-to-change-the-consensus","id":1527673,"title":"Have you ever managed to change the consensus?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-31T18:29:31-08:00","id":1527673,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Have you ever managed to change the consensus?","content":"A quick search reveals some interesting threads on the nature of the consensus, but I haven't seen any about players actually managing to change it in game. <br /> <br /> Have any of you guys managed to change the concensus in a meaningful way in one of your games? How did it change and how did you do it? <br /> <br /> If you haven't, do you have an idea that you would like to try to do so in the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T07:25:43-08:00","id":1527690,"title":"","content":"I think this would only be possible with mental magic on a global scale, or at least across an entire state, to change people's perceptions. I can only imagine the effect of the paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T11:21:07-08:00","id":1527779,"title":"","content":"It's something I've wanted to build a game around, certainly. What systems I'd use would depend greatly on how the Consensus works in your game, really. We don't have a ton of details on the mechanics of it, such as what percentage of the population needs to believe something to make it true, how long they need to believe it for, if only humans affect the consensus, etc. All that has to be decided based on the needs of the game.<br /> <br /> The interesting part, I think, would be in experiencing the effects of the change, rather than achieving the change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T00:40:26-08:00","id":1527996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527673-have-you-ever-managed-to-change-the-consensus?p=1527779#post1527779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something I've wanted to build a game around, certainly. What systems I'd use would depend greatly on how the Consensus works in your game, really. We don't have a ton of details on the mechanics of it, such as what percentage of the population needs to believe something to make it true, how long they need to believe it for, if only humans affect the consensus, etc. All that has to be decided based on the needs of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish they gave more detail. After all, if you are playing the Traditions or the Disparates, that is the name of the game, isn't it? To win the Ascension War and change the consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T09:04:02-08:00","id":1528029,"title":"","content":"In universe, though, I'm not sure the factions have a clear sense of how to do it. That is, mages know some things work - the Technocracy spends a lot of time making tech user friendly, controlling the flow of information, and discrediting the occult - but they aren't sure which ones are most effective. The Technocracy spends time and effort cleansing the Umbra of ideas it doesn't like. Is that working? No idea, but they seem to think it might.<br /> <br /> Whatever system is used shouldn't invalidate any of that. I think if I were to put together rules for it, I would use some sort of Milestone system, where a number of different tactics can be used to achieve small victories and after enough of them, there would be the opportunity for a major milestone with a functional change. After that there'd be a followup struggle to anchor the change and deal with unintended consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T10:29:15-08:00","id":1528039,"title":"","content":"Sounds a bit like the acts of Imperium in the <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> sourcebook <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>. When the <b>Operative's Dossier</b> have rules for Terranorming, it kind of skipped one crucial part: actually implementing the change. It talked about doing the prep work and capping it off afterwards, but nothing about making the change itself. For that, all we have are some notes about shifting reality zones in M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T12:40:54-08:00","id":1528046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527673-have-you-ever-managed-to-change-the-consensus?p=1527690#post1527690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this would only be possible with mental magic on a global scale, or at least across an entire state, to change people's perceptions. I can only imagine the effect of the paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the exact amount of paradox is 0, since the consensus changed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T12:53:51-08:00","id":1528048,"title":"","content":"Overall. I wouldn't allow changing the consensus by mind control, partly because it runs against the spirit of the game (in my opinion anyways) and partly because it makes the consensus and reality nonconsensual, and there's reason to think the consensus can't do that. <br /> <br /> It also depends a great deal on how and how fast the consensus changes reality. If there's metaphysical inertia, it may take quite some time before really profound changes come into effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T13:20:09-08:00","id":1528052,"title":"","content":"It also runs counter to the rules for mental influence in HDYDT, which says that any attempts at mass mind manipulation will leave a significant minority unaffected or biased the other way, because otherwise the Ascension War would have been won long ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T19:43:39-08:00","id":1528079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527673-have-you-ever-managed-to-change-the-consensus?p=1528052#post1528052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also runs counter to the rules for mental influence in HDYDT, which says that any attempts at mass mind manipulation will leave a significant minority unaffected or biased the other way, because otherwise the Ascension War would have been won long ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a significant minority is still a minority, so the general consensus would have changed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T07:27:30-08:00","id":1528105,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily. We don't know the specifics of how the Consensus operates; so it's entirely possible that you need more than just a simple majority to change the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T13:30:55-08:00","id":1528163,"title":"","content":"So, one thing that immediately springs to mind...what do you mean by 'changing the consensus'? <br /> <br /> Theoretically, we get the idea that both the Union and the Traditions are adding or changing things in the consensus to some degree, aka advanced technology is being created by the Technocracy and is gradually accepted as possible by humanity so it's added to the consensus. Just as prominently, we have a few wins from the Traditions who added things to the consensus that the Unions were not exactly happy with, but now its there its very hard to 'take it back'. <br /> <br /> I don't think mass mind control is a great way to actually change the consensus, though that's just my personal view. Datawave is right in that when your laying out huge mind effects, there are going to be people who you miss. <br /> <br /> I think at least regarding m20, the place you might want to look for how to change the consensus is the writeups of Reality Zones. M20 breaks the types of Reality Zones down into Earthly Foundations, Technocratic Reality, Local Reality and Primal Reality (though there might be more. <br /> <br /> The Earthly Foundations are regarded as the the very base level of reality. They are also very similar to a writeup in second edition, which means that they might be how reality functions 'normally', or they might just be so deeply embedded in the consensus that it is nearly impossible to root them at, and may have been put there by the Pure Ones. They cover the very simple ways reality works. Things fall down. You can't be in more than one place at once. Things proceed one after another. Things don't suddenly appear or disappear out of thin air. 1+1 =2. Very base assumptions fit here. <br /> <br /> Technocratic Reality is regarded as the general 'default assumption' in m20, though it is more prominent in cities. Advanced Technology like your cellphone or your computer work. Medicine as we understand it fits here to some degree. <br /> <br /> There is also Local reality, where in a small area (from your sanctum to a small town) you have changed the local consensus to accept a different paragdim/focus as the norm. One example in m20 was a guy from the big city going to a very remote rural town and finding out that in such a location advanced tech like his cellphone no longer functioned, but that there was a preacher healing people by praying. Finally, there is 'Primal Reality' which the traditions hold was in place before the Technocrats started imposing their own view of reality, I forget the function of what it did though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T13:59:17-08:00","id":1528166,"title":"","content":"I have a whole post on my thoughts about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus\">the nature of the Consensus</a>, which might be worth reviewing if for no other reason than to have a better idea of where I'm coming from.<br /> <br /> But I would also point you to \u201cShifting the Zone\u201d (<b>M20</b> pp 615\u2013617), which gives the basics for how to go about changing a Reality Zone. And then there's \u201cTerranorming: A How-To Guide for the Can-Do Symposium\u201d (<b>The Operative's Dossier</b>, pp.92\u201393) which provides a complimentary crunchy system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T08:15:53-08:00","id":1528260,"title":"","content":"I am reminded of Terry Pratchett's Hogfather, which does have quite the bearing on this discussion albeit the metaphysics are different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T12:33:35-08:00","id":1528279,"title":"","content":"M20 has a section on the idea of changing a local consensus by shaping the local population; an example that fits with their vision of it would be a local temple changing the reality zone of the block by improving the lives of the residents and making them sincerely believe in the wisdom of the monks/hippies/priestesses/whatever there.<br /> <br /> There's a problem though.<br /> <br /> I can't imagine that the Technocracy are blind to such shifts in reality zones, or particularly enthusiastic about them.<br /> <br /> You don't even need to throw HIT MARKS at the problem. Mages can beat those. No, instead you hit the temple, or whatever it is, with scandals, bills, unpaid tax demands, arrest warrants, protests, online smears... It would take a few minutes out of a NWO desk agent's day to spoil it, if the NWO hold the kind of power they do in some versions of the metaplot... and TBQH I'm pretty sure a competent VA could do it as well, without any of the official channels of power that NWO agents can take control of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T17:27:16-08:00","id":1528464,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wished I had a system for it, a good one.<br /> And goddamn, I still find messed up how Mage until now, never had a Chronicle about this.<br /> <br /> Specially because we could be just swaying the Consensus of a neighborhood, not an entire town. This would need some form of system like Projects from V5, but done well and integrated with the Story. And we would have to have some very functional Paradigm terms. So that the ruling Paradigms are clear, and those we are working towards are just as clear. A concise and good list should be in order. As such, the ST could look to actions and plans that bit by bit make the Consesus gravitate towards that Paradigm. Like opening a free course of Hermetic Magics (which is a cult basically) and making small but felt changes to a community of people... would make Hermetic Paradigm grow.<br /> <br /> I really hope M5 does this, and focuses on it. Otherwise Mage end up being just magic guerrilla warfare between bizarre groups, with no Humanity or Society in sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T06:43:57-08:00","id":1528645,"title":"","content":"The issue with small local changes is that it pretty much has to be small in nature. You can get odd effects and odd superstitions, but nothing that would look like a really visible change. The reason being that outside specific circumstances sleepers are not staying in one small zone, they are contributing to both the small local neighborhood and the entire town.<br /> <br /> I'd also consider the changing of the reality to be less like a simple or trackable system (in universe) and more like a chaotic weather pattern of belief fronts and obstinancy vortexes. This makes changing reality possible but unpredictable and prone to unexpected phenomena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T08:16:07-08:00","id":1528651,"title":"","content":"That's reinforced by the Information Age, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"